  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes Rasengan, a gate‑based variational algorithm that expands feasible solution space using transition Hamiltonians. Across 2000 benchmark instances from five constrained‑optimization domains, Rasengan reduces circuit depth from ~7000 to ~50 and improves approximation‑ratio gap by up to 4.12× compared to prior QAOA variants, with circuits of roughly 21–87 depth on problems up to ~24 qubits and small demonstrations on IBM Kyiv and Brisbane devices.",
